 "title": "Castles Were Never Just Homes",
 "cat": "history",
 "emoji": "🏰",
 "sentences": [
  "Castles were offensive bases, not just homes.",
  "Scholars define them as private fortified residences for nobility.",
  "Unlike palaces, their primary purpose was defense and control.",
  "These structures appeared after the Carolingian Empire fell.",
  "Lords used them to control surrounding territory during raids.",
  "Common features included curtain walls, arrowslits, and portcullises.",
  "Sometimes, even modern homes are built to mimic these ancient fortresses."
